{
  "_comment": "Cyber keyword list used ONLY to promote CPV 722*/725* notices to cyber_broad (cyber_strict is CPV-only, 728*). EDITABLE. Matching is applied to the notice title in ALL languages present, after normalization: unicode accent folding (š->s, é->e, ä->a, plus ø->o, đ->d, ß->ss, æ->ae, œ->oe, ł->l), curly apostrophes -> straight. Patterns below must therefore be written accent-free. match types: 'substring' = case-insensitive containment; 'word' = case-insensitive whole word (regex word boundaries; multi-word phrases allowed); 'acronym' = CASE-SENSITIVE whole word, AND matched only when the title contains lowercase context - ALL-CAPS titles (common on TED) would make every word look like an acronym ('SOC. COOP.' is an Italian company form, not a security operations center). langs is informational. risk notes flag entries most likely to produce false positives - prune there first.",
  "keywords": [
    {"pattern": "cyber",  "match": "substring", "langs": ["en", "fr", "nl", "de", "da", "sv", "it", "es"], "note": "covers cybersecurity, cybersecurite, cyberbeveiliging, cybersikkerhed, cybersakerhet, cyberattack...; broad but applied only within CPV 722/725"},
    {"pattern": "kiber",  "match": "substring", "langs": ["hr", "lv", "lt", "hu"], "note": "kiberneticka sigurnost, kiberdrosiba, kibernetinis saugumas, kiberbiztonsag"},
    {"pattern": "kyber",  "match": "substring", "langs": ["fi", "cs", "sk"], "note": "kyberturvallisuus, kyberneticka bezpecnost"},
